# Sim page folders (`js/pages/sim/`)

`/sim/` is the first large page that **must** use section folders. Do not add new UI files on the page root. Other pages stay flat until they hit the same mess.

## Root only

| File | Why it stays |
|---|---|
| `index.js` | HTML entry |
| `page.js` | Orchestration |
| `sim.css` | Stage / field layout |
| `sim-events.js` | Shared event contract (engine + UI) |
| `sim-combat-time.js` | Shared by engine + UI |
| `demo-timeline.js` | Engine demo mode |

## Section folders

| Folder | Put here |
|---|---|
| `engine/` | Combat sim (already split). Do not move. |
| `shell/` | Boot, board load, permalink, status, runs, live tips |
| `hud/` | Combat HUD + fighter avatars |
| `fx/` | Damage numbers, item overlays, charge, item chrome |
| `log/` | Combat log, damage meter, results, logbook |
| `log-ui/` | `/sim/log-ui/` kitchen sink (separate HTML) |
| `controls/` | Scrubber, settings, round picker, premium gate |
| `foe/` | Dummy / public build / mirror, rails, build browser |
| `report/` | In-page issue report |

Colocate that section’s `.css` next to its `.js`. HTML still loads only `index.js`.

```js
// ❌ js/pages/sim/sim-new-widget.js
// ✅ js/pages/sim/fx/sim-new-widget.js  (or hud/ log/ foe/ …)
```

When adding a **new kind** of chrome, make a new folder — do not grow the root. Keep ~500 lines / one job per file.

Other pages that import sim helpers use the section path (`../sim/shell/sim-permalink.js`, not `../sim/sim-permalink.js`).
